	<p>Welcome to Crofter Market! We are excited you are here, and we look forward to being able to grow with you at this time. The Crofter Market app, and any associated websites or other programs (“App”) are owned and operated by Crofter Market, Inc., Crofter Market, LLC, or any other subsidiary companies (“Crofter Market”, “us”, “we”, or “our”), and you agree that any potential liability or responsibility is limited to just the entity that provides the applicable service, which responsibilities and services may be updated from time to time without changing this agreement. To help ensure good communication and an understanding of our services, we have provided you as a user of this App (“you” or “your”) with the terms and conditions that govern our services and App operations (“Terms”). If you use our App, or you request any services from us, you consent to these Terms and agree that these Terms apply to govern our interactions.</p>

	<h3>Our Values and Community</h3>

	<p>At Crofter Market, we are a community of individuals and companies that share in a set of values and beliefs. If you use the App, you are agreeing that you share the same values and beliefs, which are:</p>

	<ol>
		<li>A strong and healthy decentralized food supply chain is important for individual, family, and societal health. Decentralization of the food supply chain makes it more resilient, provides better choices for consumers, and avoids monopolization.</li>
		<li>Promoting local food networks and communities helps to increase a) self-sufficiency (an important part of individual and societal health), b) security against natural disasters, c) security against supply chain attacks, and d) a reduction of poverty, and this also helps to support small farmers.</li>
		<li>All individuals have the inherent right to grow and eat their own food or food they obtain for others for the purpose of controlling their health, becoming self-sufficient, and acting with bodily autonomy.</li>
		<li>The government should not unduly restrict the ability of individuals to make knowing, informed choices about the foods they eat or consume.</li>
		<li>Regulation of food that is grown or raised, processed, and distributed all within the same state, and all such businesses associated with food production, should only be by state or local governments, not the federal government.</li>
	</ol>

	<p>Specifically, we, along with the members of our community, assert that the above rights are fundamental individual and human rights protected by State and Federal Constitutions. We fully believe that these rights are expressly and implicitly protected, including in declarations within such constitutions that there are other, unenumerated rights retained by the people. Community members fully believe that the government should not regulate or interfere in the core functions of individuals in electing their food or health choices. We authorize Crofter Market to initiate lawsuits on our behalf to protect the above values and interests.</p>

	<p>App users also fully believe and maintain that the common law and the law of nature both dictate that these rights are fundamental rights, essential in the fabric of a constitutional republic. Individuals are individual because there is not one option that works for everyone, and there are many food types that may be proper for each person. Each individual has the right and freedom to select for themselves how they nourish and cultivate their body and mind, and the members in the community have come together specifically to pursue and create a community focused on providing these opportunities to those who also hold and follow these same core values.</p>

	<p>You agree that to be an active member of our community, you will purchase or provide food to purchase on the App at least once per year. If you do not interact with and contribute to the community at least once per year in this manner, you will not be considered an active member of the community. We hope though that you choose to pursue many opportunities with the app and others in your area so that you can benefit from the amazing people, opportunities, and food sources that exist around you.</p>

	<p>If you do not agree with these values, you are not permitted to use the App or its services.</p>

	<h3>The App and Services</h3>

	<p>At Crofter Market, we strive to connect food producers with food consumers. We highly respect the food producers and the work they do, and we want to build and strengthen local and communal networks for local food distribution and consumption.</p>

	<p>It is important to note that Crofter Market does not produce food, nor does Crofter Market guarantee or warrant the food that is sold on the App. All food producers are independently owned and operated, and the App is a place to connect the Producers to the Consumers.</p>

	<p>Due to this, every Purchaser and Consumer must take steps to ensure that they are satisfied with the condition of the food or product offered and that they assume the responsibility to independently verify the quality, contents, and other material factors associated with the food or product purchased. You agree to be responsible for these items and for your own health and safety. You specifically agree that you are not relying on anything from the App or Crofter Market related to your decisions in purchasing or consuming the food or products offered for sale and that you are fully responsible for your own choices and decisions.</p>

